## PRACTICAL INTELLIGENCE

### Day 1 Actions
1. Pick ONE niche market you already know (construction materials, F&B supplies, used equipment, agricultural inputs — whatever you have existing knowledge of)
2. Open Zalo group for that niche. Name it descriptively: "[Niche] Ket Noi Mua Ban [City]"
3. Post 3 useful market observations (prices, availability, quality notes) — VALUE FIRST

### Day 3 Actions
1. Contact 5 suppliers in your niche via Zalo/phone. Ask: "Anh/chi co hang gi can ban gap khong?" (urgent inventory)
2. Contact 5 potential buyers. Ask: "Anh/chi dang can gi ma chua tim duoc?" (unmet needs)
3. Match 1 supplier to 1 buyer. Ask for referral fee or margin.

### Day 7 Actions
1. First deal closed or pipeline of 3+ potential matches
2. Calculate: time spent vs revenue generated. If <$2/hr equivalent → pivot niche, not model
3. Document: what information was hardest to find? That is where your value is highest.

### Kill Criteria (30-day gate)
- 0 deals closed in 30 days → KILL this niche (not model — try different niche)
- Revenue < $50/month after 60 days across 2 niches → KILL model, try #3 or #10
- >8 hours/day required with no delegation path visible → model is a JOB, not a business

