## RISK FACTORS

1. **[RISK:AI_DISRUPTION]** Models #6 (VA), #1 (digitization) highly vulnerable to AI replacement. Model #8 (content) partially vulnerable — VN-language content less affected than English.
2. **Labor trap:** 7 of 12 models hit HARD CAP (Q4=NO + Q5=LABOR). Without deliberate staircase transition, founder builds a job not a business.
3. **Network dependency:** Top models (#12, #3) require relationship capital that takes months to build. Impatient founders will abandon before compound effects kick in.
4. **Platform risk:** Model #8 depends on YouTube/TikTok algorithms. One policy change can destroy revenue overnight.
5. **Base rate:** ~85% of micro-businesses at this capital level remain at side-hustle level indefinitely [T, based on SBA small business statistics, no VN-specific data available]. The 15% that escape share one trait: systematic reinvestment of early revenue into leverage (people, systems, or content).

